	"title"		"soccer_street_arena"
	"description"		"[h1]soccer_street_arena[/h1]
A street court for CS2 SoccerMod, made for three against three: asphalt, graffiti and festival flags between a hillside of houses and a colonial street, at golden hour. Street football in Brazil.

[h2]What it is[/h2]
[list]
[*] An asphalt court of 1300 x 1800 units; walls and fences are in play and invisible walls go on above them - the ball never leaves the court
[*] Behind one goal: houses in bright colours up a hill, a tiled stairway, a statue on the peak; behind the other: a colonial street with a church, palms, and the round rock across the bay
[*] Over the court: strings of festival flags and bulbs that swing in the wind, kites over the roofs
[*] Along one side a metro viaduct on steel columns; a train runs over it every 45 seconds
[*] Goals inside two cut-open shipping containers
[*] Graffiti instead of adverts: pieces along the walls, murals at both ends, a faded sprayed painting on the ground
[*] Onlookers in street clothes on the sidewalks, the containers, the balconies, the church steps and the stairway
[*] Working radar
[/list]

[h2]Made for SoccerMod[/h2]
Kicking, goals and matches come from the CS2 SoccerMod server plugin: [url=https://github.com/Deidakom/CS2_Soccer_Mod]github.com/Deidakom/CS2_Soccer_Mod[/url]. This item carries everything the plugin shows and plays (models, sounds, menus), so a server needs no second item. Without the plugin the map loads, but the ball is only a physics prop.

[h2]Patch notes[/h2]
[b]2026-10-02[/b] First version.
"
	"changenote"		"First version."
}
